.Dd July 27, 2026
.Dt SECUREDMARC 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm securedmarc
.Nd DMARC policy evaluation milter for Postfix
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl c Ar config-file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a high-performance Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting, and
Conformance (DMARC) milter implementing RFC 7489.
It reads upstream SPF and DKIM Authentication-Results headers, evaluates
DMARC policy alignment, and adds its own Authentication-Results header
with the DMARC verdict.
.Pp
.Nm
must be placed in the milter chain after both
.Xr securespf 8
and
.Xr securedkim 8
so that their Authentication-Results headers are available for evaluation.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl c Ar config-file
Path to the INI-style configuration file.
Required.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The configuration file uses INI format with a
.Ql [global]
section and one or more
.Ql [listener:name]
sections.
.Ss Global Section
.Bl -tag -width "SyslogFacility" -compact
.It Cm AuthservID
Identifier for Authentication-Results headers.
Must match the AuthservID used by
.Nm securespf
and
.Nm securedkim
so that their results can be parsed.
Default:
.Dq localhost .
.It Cm StripAuthResults
Remove every pre-existing Authentication-Results header claiming our
.Cm AuthservID ,
not just the ones asserting a
.Li dmarc=
result.
Enable this only where no other SecureMilter daemon precedes
.Nm :
otherwise it also discards the
.Li spf=
and
.Li dkim=
results this daemon evaluates, and every message fails alignment.
Those inputs are already protected \(em
.Xr securespf 8
and
.Xr securedkim 8
each remove forged claims for their own method before adding the real one.
Default: no.
.It Cm PublicSuffixList
Path to a Public Suffix List file, used only to veto a DNS tree walk result.
Recommended for now, though not required.
.Pp
.Sy Deprecated .
This option covers the transition to RFC 9989 and is expected to be removed in
a future version.
RFC 9989 replaced the Public Suffix List with the DNS tree walk outright, and
observes that relying on a PSL
.Dq might arrive at a different answer
than the walk does, so consulting one at all is a deliberate deviation from
the standard \(em constrained here so that it can only reject a boundary the
walk selected, never select one itself.
As
.Li psd=
is published more widely the veto has less and less to reject.
Do not build anything on this option that would break when it is removed.
.Pp
Organizational domains are determined by the RFC 9989 DNS tree walk:
.Nm
walks up
.Li _dmarc.<name>
and each zone declares its own boundary with the
.Li psd=
tag, so no external list is needed and
.Nm
is correct without one.
The walk's last resort, however, is the shortest name that published a DMARC
record, which assumes a public suffix publishing DMARC also publishes
.Li psd=y .
RFC 9989 is recent and
.Li psd=
is not yet widely deployed, so a registry publishing a record without the tag
would be chosen as an organizational domain shared by every registrant beneath
it — the boundary collapse that lets
.Li attacker.co.uk
align with
.Li victim.co.uk .
Setting this option rejects such a boundary.
The list may only reject a boundary, never choose one, and
.Nm
falls back to the tree walk alone when the option is unset or the file cannot
be read; which mode is in effect is reported at startup.
.Pp
Install the list from packages with
.Dl pkg install public_suffix_list
which provides
.Pa /usr/local/share/public_suffix_list/public_suffix_list.dat ,
or download it from
.Lk https://publicsuffix.org/list/
(MPL 2.0) and point this option at it.
The file is parsed once at startup: rules are one per line, with
.Ql //
comments,
.Ql *
wildcard labels and
.Ql \&!
exceptions.
Because the list changes as registries come and go, refresh it periodically
and restart
.Nm
afterwards —
.Dv SIGHUP
does not reload it.
Default: unset.
.It Cm WorkerThreads
Number of worker threads.
0 means auto-detect CPU count.
Default: 0.
.It Cm PidFile
Path to the PID file.
Default:
.Pa /var/run/securedmarc/securedmarc.pid .
.It Cm Foreground
Run in foreground without daemonizing.
Default: no.
.It Cm User
Drop privileges to this user after binding sockets.
.It Cm Syslog
Enable syslog output.
Default: yes.
.It Cm SyslogFacility
Syslog facility.
Default: mail.
.It Cm LogLevel
Logging verbosity: err, warn, info, debug.
Default: info.
.It Cm DnsNameserver
Comma-separated DNS nameserver IPs.
Default:
.Dq 127.0.0.1 .
.It Cm DnsTimeout
DNS query timeout in seconds.
Default: 5.
.It Cm DnsRetries
Number of DNS query retries.
Default: 2.
.It Cm DnsCacheSize
Maximum DNS cache entries per worker.
Default: 1000.
.It Cm DnsNegativeTTL
Negative cache TTL in seconds.
Default: 60.
.It Cm MaxHeaders
Largest number of headers accumulated for one message.
Default: 500.
0 disables the limit.
.It Cm MaxHeaderBytes
Largest total header size, names plus values, accumulated for one message.
Accepts an optional
.Cm K , Cm M
or
.Cm G
suffix.
Default: 1M.
0 disables the limit.
.Pp
DMARC is evaluated from the
.Cm From
header together with the
.Cm spf=
and
.Cm dkim=
results added earlier in the milter chain, so
.Nm
never buffers a message body and has no
.Cm MaxBodyBytes .
The header block is precisely what it reads.
.Pp
A message exceeding either limit is tempfailed rather than delivered.
Headers past the limit are never read, so neither a forged
.Cm Authentication-Results
nor a second
.Cm From
header hidden beyond the limit could be acted on.
Raise these if legitimate mail crossing many forwarders and mailing lists is
being deferred.
Both are read at startup only;
.Dv SIGHUP
does not change them.
.It Cm ZmqEndpoint
ZeroMQ PUB endpoint for event publishing.
Disabled if not set.
.It Cm ZmqTopic
ZeroMQ topic prefix.
Default:
.Dq dmarc.evaluation .
.El
.Ss Listener Sections
Each
.Ql [listener:name]
section defines a socket to listen on.
.Bl -tag -width "Socket" -compact
.It Cm Socket
Listen address.
Format:
.Dq inet:port@ip
or
.Dq unix:/path .
The
.Ar ip
must be a numeric IPv4 or IPv6 address; no name resolution is performed.
A value that cannot be parsed is a fatal configuration error and is reported
with the section that contains it \(em it is never ignored, and never falls
back to the default listener.
.El
.Pp
If no listener sections are defined, the default is
.Dq inet:8894@127.0.0.1 ,
loopback only.
.Pp
The milter protocol carries no authentication, so any client that can reach this
socket is trusted completely, and this daemon is the one that decides disposition.
The caller supplies the
.Va Authentication-Results
fields this daemon evaluates, so a reachable socket defeats DMARC without needing
to forge a header in transit, and under
.Dv p=reject
it decides which mail is refused.
Only the local MTA should ever connect.
Bind a routable address only when the MTA runs on a different machine, and
restrict access to it with
.Xr pf 4 .
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width "SIGTERM" -compact
.It Dv SIGHUP
Reload configuration.
.It Dv SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown with 30 second drain timeout.
.El
.Sh POSTFIX INTEGRATION
.Nm
must be ordered after SPF and DKIM milters:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
smtpd_milters = inet:127.0.0.1:8890,
                inet:127.0.0.1:8891,
                inet:127.0.0.1:8894
milter_connect_macros = j {daemon_name} v {client_addr}
milter_default_action = accept
.Ed
.Sh LOG FORMAT
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securedmarc[pid]: id=QUEUEID peer=HOST[IP] client=IP domain=DOMAIN elapsed=Nms
.Ed
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/etc/securedmarc/securedmarc.conf"
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/securedmarc/securedmarc.conf
Default configuration file.
.It Pa /var/run/securedmarc/securedmarc.pid
Default PID file.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/public_suffix_list/public_suffix_list.dat
Public Suffix List as installed by the
.Pa dns/public_suffix_list
package, for use with
.Cm PublicSuffixList .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr securespf 8 ,
.Xr securedkim 8 ,
.Xr securearc 8
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting, and Conformance (DMARC)
.%R RFC 7489
.Re
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Daniel Morante
